WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:05.779
When Crypto’s golden boy lost his entire
empire overnight, instead of running away

00:00:05.779 --> 00:00:08.830
from the spotlight, he ran towards it.

00:00:08.830 --> 00:00:11.620
Appearing in interview after interview.

00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:14.839
I’m deeply sorry about what happened.

00:00:14.839 --> 00:00:18.759
I’ve had a bad month.

00:00:18.759 --> 00:00:20.880
That is an understatement.

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:24.369
He showed signs of nervousness in this New
York Times interview.

00:00:24.369 --> 00:00:29.359
Perhaps the gravity of a scandal that could
be bigger than Enron hit him.

00:00:29.359 --> 00:00:34.940
Many wondered why in the world he wasn’t
arrested right away after losing billions

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:41.300
of dollars of customer funds when his cryptocurrency
exchange FTX collapsed in November.

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:48.270
It wasn’t until exactly one month, and one
day after FTX filed for bankruptcy, that police

00:00:48.270 --> 00:00:54.320
in the Bahamas arrested SBF in his luxury
home he shared with roommates…at the request

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:56.109
of the U.S.

00:00:56.109 --> 00:00:59.800
Hours before, SBF had been playing a video
game.

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:00.800
(Storybook brawl)

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:05.460
The Securities and Exchange Commission has
charged him with defrauding big investors

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:09.100
who committed nearly $2 billion in recent
years.

00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:12.619
SEC’s chairman Gary Gensler said in a statement:

00:01:12.619 --> 00:01:19.100
“We allege that Sam Bankman-Fried built
a house of cards on a foundation of deception

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:24.299
while telling investors that it was one of
the safest buildings in crypto.”

00:01:24.299 --> 00:01:31.100
Sam Bankman-Fried reportedly used billions
in customer funds from FTX to prop up his

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:36.880
other company, Alameda Research, a hedge fund
that was in trouble after trying to bail out

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:39.619
other struggling crypto firms.

00:01:39.619 --> 00:01:45.340
He reportedly built a “back door” in FTX’s
accounting software that let him move billions

00:01:45.340 --> 00:01:52.340
of dollars from FTX to Alameda without flagging
the transactions to external auditors.

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:56.280
SBF has repeatedly denied that he did anything
wrong.

00:01:56.280 --> 00:02:02.890
Did you know these funds were being funneled
to Alameda, what is your answer?

00:02:02.890 --> 00:02:12.270
I did not know there was any improper use
of customer funds.

00:02:12.270 --> 00:02:18.610
When the crypto website CoinDesk revealed
the close ties between SBF’s two companies,

00:02:18.610 --> 00:02:23.510
FTX and Alameda, that made Binance nervous.

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:29.070
Binance is the world’s largest cryptocurrency
exchange that was an early investor in FTX.

00:02:29.070 --> 00:02:35.480
And subsequently sold its stake in FTX, consisting
mainly of the FTX token FTT.

00:02:35.480 --> 00:02:36.540
($580 million)

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:41.709
That caused the price of the token to plummet
and resulted in a domino effect of nervous

00:02:41.709 --> 00:02:46.909
customers pulling out…leading to the spectacular
fall of FTX, which I covered in more detail

00:02:46.909 --> 00:02:47.909
in another video.

00:02:47.909 --> 00:02:53.030
Along the way, billions of dollars of customers’
funds also went missing.

00:02:53.030 --> 00:02:57.960
Bankman-Fried has said that if he'd spent
'an hour a day' thinking about risk management

00:02:57.960 --> 00:03:00.909
FTX might not have collapsed.

00:03:00.909 --> 00:03:03.489
His companies thrived on risk.

00:03:03.489 --> 00:03:09.659
Risk was baked into his company Alameda, whose
CEO was his ex-girlfriend Caroline Ellison,

00:03:09.659 --> 00:03:12.520
a 28-year-old Harry Potter-loving math whiz.

00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:13.520
This is how she described her business mentality.

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:18.120
I think being comfortable with risk is very
important.

00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:22.739
We tend not to have things like stop losses.

00:03:22.739 --> 00:03:26.160
I think those aren’t necessarily a great
risk management tool.

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:31.670
A stop-loss is designed to limit the maximum
loss of a trade by automatically selling an

00:03:31.670 --> 00:03:34.780
asset once it reaches a certain value.

00:03:34.780 --> 00:03:38.709
Not having a stop loss is INCREDIBLY risky.

00:03:38.709 --> 00:03:41.459
Yet no one saw the signs of doom.

00:03:41.459 --> 00:03:44.860
SBF and his team had everyone fooled.

00:03:44.860 --> 00:03:47.489
He was called the next Warren Buffett.

00:03:47.489 --> 00:03:52.430
It certainly didn’t help that superstars
like Tom Brady and Stephen Curry vouched for

00:03:52.430 --> 00:03:53.430
FTX.

00:03:53.430 --> 00:03:57.670
With FTX I have everything I need to buy,
sell, and trade crypto safely.

00:03:57.670 --> 00:04:04.069
The glitz and glamour hid what some FTX users
call a Ponzi scheme….in which the first

00:04:04.069 --> 00:04:09.140
investors are rewarded with money that’s
actually been invested by later investors,

00:04:09.140 --> 00:04:12.959
rather than making money from a legitimate
product or service.

00:04:12.959 --> 00:04:18.519
The mastermind of a massive Ponzi scheme,
Bernie Madoff, ripped off tens of thousands

00:04:18.519 --> 00:04:21.880
of people of as much as $65 billion.

00:04:21.880 --> 00:04:26.380
Madoff was sentenced to 150 years in prison.

00:04:26.380 --> 00:04:29.949
Could SBF suffer the same fate?

00:04:29.949 --> 00:04:35.330
He is set to be extradited to the U.S., where
federal prosecutors are charging him with

00:04:35.330 --> 00:04:41.860
wire fraud, wire fraud conspiracy, securities
fraud, securities fraud conspiracy, money

00:04:41.860 --> 00:04:42.860
laundering.

00:04:42.860 --> 00:04:46.759
AND, violating campaign finance laws.

00:04:46.759 --> 00:04:52.410
He was the darling of the Democrats, donating
millions to them…though he now says he secretly

00:04:52.410 --> 00:04:55.880
gave roughly the same amount to Republicans.

00:04:55.880 --> 00:05:03.060
If convicted, he faces a maximum sentence
of 115 years.

00:05:03.060 --> 00:05:08.830
The fall of one of the largest cryptocurrency
exchanges is another nail in the coffin of

00:05:08.830 --> 00:05:14.419
an already fragile crypto market that has
yet to recover from the crash in the spring.

00:05:14.419 --> 00:05:16.870
Can people trust crypto ever again?

00:05:16.870 --> 00:05:19.040
Is Binance safe?

00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:25.210
The U.S. Department of Justice has been investigating
Binance since 2018, including its founder

00:05:25.210 --> 00:05:26.550
Changpeng Zhao.

00:05:26.550 --> 00:05:32.069
Reuters reported that it has to do with Binance's
compliance with U.S. anti-money laundering

00:05:32.069 --> 00:05:34.539
laws and sanctions.

